because \(x\ne0\). The polynomial \(q\) is monic of degree two.
Therefore the coefficient of \(A^{r+2}V\) in the resulting block-power
expansion of \(q(A)x\) is exactly \(c_r\ne0\).

Since \(k+1\le j\le s\), the block Krylov matrix \[
[V,AV,\ldots,A^kV]
